questions.code:
CREATE INDEX orders_data_gin ON orders USING gin (data);

SELECT id FROM orders
WHERE data ->> 'sku' = 'ABC-1'
  AND data ->> 'qty' > '10';

questions.answer:
`->>` comparisons are not supported by GIN, so it seq-scans; and `data ->> 'qty' > '10'` compares text ('9' > '10'). Use containment for equality and cast numbers, with expression indexes as needed.
```sql
CREATE INDEX orders_sku_idx ON orders ((data ->> 'sku'));
CREATE INDEX orders_qty_idx ON orders (((data ->> 'qty')::int));
SELECT id FROM orders
WHERE data ->> 'sku' = 'ABC-1' AND (data ->> 'qty')::int > 10;
-- or: WHERE data @> '{"sku":"ABC-1"}' using the GIN index
```
